# Zone 1, room 7: Coyote dash (BUILD.md s5, the twelve core tech interactions, 7: "dash off a ledge
# within coyote time keeps ground cooldown rules. Taught by a cliff"; docs/adr/0010, Dash: a dash
# within 6 frames of walking off a ledge is a ground dash, so the air dash stays in hand).
# Grey box (Phase 1), not art. 60 x 34 tiles, floor top at y 864, doors 128 u tall (y 736 to 864).
#
# The way: arrival plateau (x 0 to 384, open above), then a tunnel under a stand-in "overhang", a
# solid box 44 u over the floor (the standing body's height: a jump cannot climb, so the cliff
# asks for dashes, not height). Under it, left to right:
#   - Trench A (x 576 to 768): the safe first encounter. 32 u deep, solid floor, no hazard: a
#     ground dash from its edge crosses it (z1_07_coyote_dash, frame 58), and walking in costs one
#     jump back out (the roof leaves exactly enough room).
#   - The island (x 768 to 992), a run-up.
#   - Chasm B (x 992 to 1604, 612 u): a row of pit tiles 32 u under the floor, the far ledge's lip
#     at x 1604 (a box flush with the floor, x 1604 to 1632; smooth, no cling). The tech: walk off
#     the edge, dash on one of the first 6 airborne ticks (the coyote dash: horizontal, ground
#     cooldown, air dash untouched), air dash about 16 to 17 frames later and air jump about 24 to
#     25 frames after the first dash (on the air dash's last frames, a dash-jump) to lift from the
#     pit's lip to the ledge.
#   - The far ledge under the roof to x 1664, then open sky and the east door (x 1920).
#
# Ticks, from the edge. Ash runs at 9 u a tick and the floor ends under her during one tick (94
# in z1_07_coyote_dash, from spawn 74: x 997.5 after tick 93, 1006.5 after tick 94). A dash read on
# that tick finds her on the floor: it is an ordinary ground dash, with the same cooldown and air
# dash as a coyote dash, and it starts as far along as any ground dash can. The coyote window is
# the 6 ticks after it (95 to 100); a dash on 101 is the air dash. The first version of this room
# set its control on tick 93 and the lip 14 u past that route's reach: a dash on 94 crosses it
# (movement review: tech skippable), because the run's phase moves the last grounded x by up to
# 9 u and the lip was set against one phase.
#
# Why it is built this way, and what it is not. The dash is flat and the roof is low, so every
# route over B is made of dashes; what a coyote dash adds over a dash read on the last tick on the
# floor is the few ticks of running past the edge (9 u a tick, up to 54 u). Measured on this room by
# tools/replay/coyote_scan.gd (every plan holds right and presses a first dash, a second dash 12 to
# 20 ticks later or none, and a jump 12 to 36 ticks after the first, held; the first dash from the
# last ticks on the floor to the sixth airborne tick; all nine phases of the run, since the
# floor ends at a different x for each; a crossing is standing on the far side): a first dash read
# on the floor (ticks 93 and 94) crosses a lip at x 1590 or nearer (598 u) and none a lip at 1594
# or farther; a coyote dash crosses a lip at 1622 (630 u) at the best phase (2 plans, 5 at 1616),
# and this one at 1604 with 6 to 10 plans for each phase. Up-right second dashes, earlier ground dashes (to 4 ticks before
# the last) and standing starts from every spawn on the island from x 800 to 860 add no
# crossing (scan results in the feel log). The lip, 14 u past the farthest ground route and 18 u
# short of the farthest coyote one (to the nearest 6 u), is where the two differ by the width of a few ticks of
# running, which is all there is to teach. It is NOT proven the only way: a search is not a proof,
# and the Ember Toss (gap_reach.gd: a toss carries a route past a tech 2 sized gap) was only
# tried once (a throw from the edge stopped about 90 u out) and not searched. Flagged for the
# director: play it, and if anything else crosses, move the lip box (x 1604) farther out.
# Fixtures: tests/replay/zone1/07_*.
room zone1/07_coyote_dash
size 60 34
